# Wedge product path

Canonical docs: `docs/product/overview.md`, `docs/product/roadmap.md`, `docs/product/phases/v*.md`.

## What Wedge is

macOS **menu-bar only** utility (OneThing-adjacent). **Requires macOS 15 Sequoia** or later. The bar shows the **one thing** (list index 0). Everything else is **Up next**, ordered by drag. Position = priority — no priority fields. **Done** (pop + sound) is the emotional core.

## Language

**one thing** · **Up next** · **Done** — not push/pop/stack/P0. Empty bar: **icon only**. Non-empty: **title only** (no circle).

UI copy constants: `wedge/Copy/WedgeCopy.swift` (change naming in one place).

## Horizon

**v1 → v2 → v3 only** (all shipped). No v4. No cloud/sync/accounts. No Dock mode. No confetti.

## v1 (shipped)

- Compact floating **panel** on left click (centered on screen, add field focused; window title **Wedge**); single list with Notion-style **6-dot drag grips**; add always to bottom of Up next.
- Inline edit: tap row text → focused `TextField` (not always-on fields inside `List`).
- Done: ⌘↩ (panel key), ⌥+click, right-click menu (no Force-click; no panel Done button).
- Persist locally. **Launch at login.**
- **Max 40 characters** per item; enforce limit; **no truncation/ellipsis logic**.
- **Minimal Settings:** native **⌘,** / **Settings…**. Menu-bar one-thing **bold** + **color**.
- See `docs/product/phases/v1.md`. Tag: **v1.0.0**.

## v2 (shipped)

- Global hotkeys: defaults **⌃⌥W** toggle panel, **⌃⌥D** Done; **remappable in Settings**.
- Denser panel keyboard: list selection ↑/↓, ⌫ delete selected when not editing.
- See `docs/product/phases/v2.md`. Tag: **v2.0.0**.

## v3 (shipped)

- **Pop sound:** on/off (default on; Done silent when off); optional custom file ≤ **3 s** (Choose… / Use default / Preview).
- **Launch at login:** Settings toggle (General).
- Status-item menu shows remappable Done shortcut.
- See `docs/product/phases/v3.md`. Tag: **v3.0.0**.

## Alignment

On any confirmed product change, update the matching phase doc + this rule (`wedge-keep-aligned`). Do not invent v4 without explicit confirmation.
